# Calliope C2 - prompt caching on the tool-call path. Issue #2170, epic #2168.
# Specced from live probes of main d812e04b, not from the issue text.
# Probe facts the waves depend on:
#  - buildParserSystemPrompt already RETURNS (cacheablePrefix, perRequestTail); parser.go:342/773.
#    agent_conductor.go:201 collapses them back into one string, then appends the budget block
#    and conductorToolInstruction AFTER the volatile tail.
#  - conductorToolInstruction says it supersedes the "Return ONLY JSON" instruction, which lives
#    in the PREFIX (parser.go body), so moving it directly after the prefix keeps "above" correct.
#  - languageDirective is a const (language.go:18), so the prefix is genuinely byte-stable.
#  - SendCachedMessage (claude.go:305) is the working two-block cache pattern to copy.
#  - TestParser_CacheablePrefix_StableAcrossCalls (parser_test.go:1868) already guards the parser
#    prefix and must stay GREEN. Do not duplicate or force it RED.
#  - SendToolMessage has 5 call sites: the interface (claude.go:31), Client, two registry wrappers
#    (registry.go:270/312), DoToolCall (retry.go:533), and the IATA resolver (iata_llm.go:224).
1 | test-engineer | ADD failing tests for issue #2170 in apps/api/internal/service/ on branch feat/calliope-c2-prompt-caching. Assert on the CONDUCTOR assembly, not the parser prompt. RED case one: the stable half of the Conductor system prompt must be byte-identical across two ParseNaturalLanguage assemblies that differ only in today date, flow, current fields JSON and refinement block; today it is not, because agent_conductor.go:201 concatenates prefix and tail and then appends conductorToolInstruction after the volatile tail. RED case two: the stable half must CONTAIN conductorToolInstruction and must NOT contain any per-request marker such as the PER-REQUEST CONTEXT header, today date, CURRENTLY FILLED FIELDS, or the BUDGET_FEASIBILITY block. Expose whatever minimal seam the assertions need rather than reaching into unexported state. Do NOT touch TestParser_CacheablePrefix_StableAcrossCalls at parser_test.go:1868 and do NOT force it RED - it already passes and guards the parser prefix. Write no production code. Read issue #2170 first. | feat/calliope-c2-prompt-caching
2 | go-backend | IMPLEMENT tool-call prompt caching for issue #2170 on branch feat/calliope-c2-prompt-caching so the wave 1 RED cases turn GREEN. Two changes. First, in agent_conductor.go stop collapsing the split: assemble the STABLE block as cacheablePrefix followed by conductorToolInstruction, and the VOLATILE block as perRequestTail followed by the budget feasibility block. This ordering is semantically safe because the Return ONLY JSON instruction that conductorToolInstruction supersedes lives in the prefix. Second, give the tool-call path a cached variant that sets a cache breakpoint on the stable system block and on the tool definitions, modelled on the existing SendCachedMessage at claude.go:305. Prefer an additive surface over changing the SendToolMessage signature in place, because the IATA resolver at iata_llm.go:224 and both registry wrappers at registry.go:270 and 312 also implement or call it and must keep working unchanged. Extraction behaviour must not change: the existing parser and conductor test suites stay GREEN. Open a PR and link issue #2170. Read issue #2170 first. | feat/calliope-c2-prompt-caching
3 | backend-critic | CRITIC ONLY on the PR for branch feat/calliope-c2-prompt-caching issue #2170. Cache correctness fails silently, so verify by inspection that no per-request value can reach the cached block, that the breakpoint sits on stable content rather than on the volatile tail, and that the reorder did not change what the model is actually told - specifically that conductorToolInstruction still follows the Return ONLY JSON instruction it supersedes. Confirm the IATA resolver and both registry wrappers still compile and behave unchanged. Confirm TestParser_CacheablePrefix_StableAcrossCalls was not modified. Executable findings only. Output VERDICT APPROVE or REVISE in handoff. Comment on the PR. Do not re-implement. | feat/calliope-c2-prompt-caching
